<title>SINGAPORE: Raffles Medical debuts at high of S$0.50.</title>
<headline>Raffles Medical debuts at high of S$0.50.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raffles Medical Group hit a high of Singapore $0.50 at its debut on Friday against its initial offer price of S$0.38.  </p>
<p>After about 13 minutes of trading, the stock was changing hands at S$0.505 and the lowest trade was at S$0.45. Total volume was a brisk 8.5 million shares.</p>
<p>Raffles, which offers primary healthcare services through a network of clinics in Singapore, had offered 38.04 million shares in its share offer to raise about S$13.5 million.</p>
<p>The offer was 50 times subscribed.</p>
<p>Raffles plans to use the funds raised for its overseas expansion.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
